  "id": "admission-criteria",
  "term": "admission criteria",
  "definition": "Admission criteria are the standards used to decide whether a person should be accepted for a service such as intensive care. In this context, they are meant to identify who is likely to benefit from admission so resources are used appropriately and unnecessarily burdensome interventions are avoided.",
